@id n3_lane_woman
# DRAFT
# Margery in the lane at dusk (night 3), her basket on her arm, hurrying home before dark.
# Night 3 keeps its own; the other nights are game/chapters/common/lane/margery.talk. She names herself, in case he never met her.
== start
(A woman with a covered basket on her arm, walking fast.)
Margery {wary}: Margery, brother, from by Saint Andrew's, if you've forgotten. I'm not stopping. Not this week.
* Where are you off to in such a hurry, Margery? -> home
* What does the lane say about the abbey? -> abbey
* Good night, Margery. -> end

== home
Margery {afraid}: Home, where else? Before Gib lights the lanterns, with the door barred and the shutters too.
Margery {amused}: My husband laughs at me for it. He can laugh from behind a barred door.
-> end

== abbey
Margery {wary}: That a holy brother hanged himself in your bell tower. Or the devil hanged him, your abbot says.
Margery {afraid}: Devil or rope, brother, he's dead all the same. And I'm late.
-> end
